On Nov 25, 8:30 pm, derekt75 <derek.truesd...@anritsu.com> wrote:
>
> Fortunately, Titans are somewhat easier to kill.

True.  Mid-game characters encountering them
for the first time can have trouble getting close
enough to kill them, due to all the nasties they
summon (and their tendency to summon more
rather than actually approach the player), but a
late-game character who has genocided or
extincted most other nasties is likely to be
able to manage it.

> Regardless of the role and alignment, I prefer
> a +7 Grayswandir.

Well, sure. There are some other artifact
weapons that I'll keep using if I have them,
rather than spend a wish on Grayswandir.
Excalibur is high on this list, and lawful
characters can often get it before the
opportunity arises to wish for anything.
Its damage isn't as high as Grayswandir,
but it's good enough (notably, there are
no "resistant" monsters who are immune
to its bonuses), and its other benefits are
more useful than hallucination resistance
(especially if you have a unicorn horn).  So
if I have it, I generally just keep using it,
rather than spend a wish on a weapon.
Magicbane is more arguable, but if I'm
playing as primarily a spellcaster I tend
to keep it for the MR and curse deflection.


